                "text": "What is the docuctl command to configure an automated 10% canary traffic split during deploy? We are on docuctl 2.0."
              }
            ],
            "role": "user"
          },
          "final_response": {
            "parts": [
              {
                "text": "In docuctl 2.0, there is no command to configure an automated canary traffic split. `docuctl` does not support canary deployments or traffic splitting. \n\nDeploys are performed using:\n\n```bash\ndocuctl deploy --env <environment>\n```\n\nFor production, all traffic switches to the new release once approved via `docuctl approve <release>`."
              }
            ],
            "role": "model"
          },
